VeridianOS: use endFilterChange() instead of invalidateRowsFilter()

GCC reported -Wdeprecated-declarations for
QSortFilterProxyModel::invalidateRowsFilter() in
MenuProxyModel::setShowIrrelevantModules() (app/MenuProxyModel.cpp): "Use
begin/endFilterChange(QSortFilterProxyModel::Direction::Rows) instead".
The function already calls beginFilterChange() before changing the filter
state; it now closes with endFilterChange(Direction::Rows). In Qt both
invalidateRowsFilter() and endFilterChange(Rows) call
filter_changed(Direction::Rows), so behaviour is unchanged.
(QSortFilterProxyModel::Direction needs Qt 6.10; the build uses 6.12.)

diff -ru a/app/MenuProxyModel.cpp b/app/MenuProxyModel.cpp
--- a/app/MenuProxyModel.cpp	2026-10-08 17:29:57.608323463 -0400
+++ b/app/MenuProxyModel.cpp	2026-10-08 17:30:26.084810961 -0400
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@
     }
     beginFilterChange(); // Qt 6.9 API
     m_showIrrelevantModules = show;
-    invalidateRowsFilter();
+    endFilterChange(QSortFilterProxyModel::Direction::Rows);
 }
 
 bool MenuProxyModel::showIrrelevantModules() const
